 Registry: Core §8.8. Codes are positive (PLCopen ErrorID is unsigned).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TASK_OVERRUN</Text><Enum>10</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ── System 10–22: controller & clock health (Core §8.12, §2.7) ──]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TASK_JITTER_HIGH</Text><Enum>11</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CPU_LOAD_HIGH</Text><Enum>12</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MEMORY_LOW</Text><Enum>13</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPC_TEMP_HIGH</Text><Enum>14</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FIELDBUS_MASTER_FAULT</Text><Enum>15</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DC_SYNC_LOST</Text><Enum>16</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TIME_SYNC_LOST</Text><Enum>17</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>UTILITY_DEVIATION</Text><Enum>18</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IPC_FAN_FAULT</Text><Enum>19</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>STORAGE_HEALTH_LOW</Text><Enum>20</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONTROLLER_METRICS_UNAVAILABLE</Text><Enum>21</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONTROLLER_MAINTENANCE_DEMANDED</Text><Enum>22</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ the controller itself demands maintenance; an engineering-tool force job is one cause]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TIMEOUT</Text><Enum>2001</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ── Framework 2000–2009: common flow reasons (Core §8.8) ──]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PERMISSIVE_NOT_MET</Text><Enum>2002</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>INTERLOCK_DROPPED</Text><Enum>2003</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RECIPE_INVALID</Text><Enum>2004</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>STEP_STALLED</Text><Enum>2005</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RETRY_EXHAUSTED</Text><Enum>2006</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CYCLE_TIME_DEGRADED</Text><Enum>2007</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ maintenance event on timing drift (Core §8.11.4(d)/§8.12)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>UNSUPPORTED_COMMAND</Text><Enum>2008</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ command outside the type's supported set (§5.6)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LINK_TIMEOUT</Text><Enum>2010</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ── Framework 2010–2019: external device / link supervision (Core §3.15) ──]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DEVICE_NOT_READY</Text><Enum>2011</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DEVICE_PROTOCOL_ERROR</Text><Enum>2012</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CARRIER_READ_FAILED</Text><Enum>2020</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ── Framework 2020–2029: traceability / part context (Core §3.16) ──]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CARRIER_WRITE_FAILED</Text><Enum>2021</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PART_ID_MISMATCH</Text><Enum>2022</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RESULT_RECORD_REJECTED</Text><Enum>2023</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EVENT_PART_RECEIVED</Text><Enum>2024</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.3 canonical part-lifecycle events (MESSAGE ring entries, not faults)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EVENT_PART_PROCESSING_STARTED</Text><Enum>2025</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EVENT_PART_PROCESSED</Text><Enum>2026</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EVENT_PART_PROCESSING_ABORTED</Text><Enum>2027</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>NOK_LIMIT_REACHED</Text><Enum>2028</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.16.5 the Unit's NOK-part limit tripped (MANUAL_RESET; Start refused)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>COMMISSIONING_GATE_ACTIVE</Text><Enum>2030</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ── Framework 2030–2039: engineering / commissioning build gates (Core §7.5) ──
 One LOW/SYSTEM event per ACTIVE gate: not clearable, not shelvable, and
 AUTO_RESET so it never blocks the commissioning it exists to serve.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONFIG_RESTORE_LOST</Text><Enum>2040</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ ── Framework 2040–2049: configuration persistence & parameter sets (§3.8b) ──
