 because a declared condition is unsatisfied (ISA-88 HELD). It is NOT a fault:
 outputs are withdrawn, the reason is published at LOW severity, and progress
 resumes by itself when the condition returns. The parent reads this to explain
 the wait instead of reporting a generic stall (§6.9).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getModuleType</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ModuleType</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getName</Name><ReturnType>STRING(80)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>648</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getState</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ExecState</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>AbortRecipe</Name></Method><Method><Name>CommitRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Infallible bounded publication after a successful PrepareRecipe.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>Cyclic</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>GetFaultSummary</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ recursive first-out walk (Core §8.2, §6.9)]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_ReleaseCommand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.1/§8.3(b) — release a command the owner can no longer complete, so the
 inherited Execute-drop reset can clear a latched terminal state. A parent needs
 this generically: when a mode chain freezes on a fault it stops polling the
 children it commanded, and a child whose Execute stays asserted can never be
 re-issued (no rising edge) nor reset (the drop reset needs Execute low).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>PrepareRecipe</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Load/validate into staging only; active ParCfg remains unchanged.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Model</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceId</Name><Value>1420</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8a/§3.10.2 — persistent configuration ownership class.
 Ordinals are an append-only PLC/HMI transport contract.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>PAR_CFG</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>STATION_CFG</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LINE_CFG</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8e shared by every station on a line; one owner]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b — the header of one named parameter set: everything needed to
 decide whether this set belongs on this machine BEFORE any value changes.

 RootIdentity and ConfigRev are the two that matter. A set taken from another
 root, or at a revision whose capabilities have since changed meaning, is not
 a set this root can silently replay - and the difference is only visible if
 the set says where and when it came from.]]></Comment><BitSize>2016</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Used</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ slot occupied (a store publishes a bounded table)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RootIdentity</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ canonical identity of the root that produced it]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>656</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SetSchema</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ set-document schema version (§13)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1312</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ConfigRev</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.10.2 manifest revision it was taken at]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1344</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ STATION_CFG = station set; PAR_CFG = model set]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1376</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ModelCode</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ model set only; '' for a station set]]></Comment><BitSize>520</BitSize><BitOffs>1408</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RecordCount</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1936</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CreatedAt</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §2.7 synchronized clock]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1952</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TimeSynchronized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ quality of CreatedAt; FALSE = display as untrusted]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1984</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigStore</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b — the medium behind an I_ConfigStore implementation, published so
 an operator can see WHERE this station's parameter sets actually live before
 trusting that a save survived. The store moves records and nothing else: it
 does not validate, does not know what a value means, and is never an
 authorization authority (§5.6, §14).
 Ordinals are an append-only PLC/HMI transport contract.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>LOCAL_RETAIN</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ in-PLC retentive memory (FB_LocalConfigStore, the shipped default)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FILE_JSON</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ controller/host file system, serialized set document]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FILE_XML</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EXTERNAL</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ database, asset system or MES behind a §3.15 connector]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigValueType</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8a/§3.10.2 — configuration value representation accepted by the
 owning typed write handler. Ordinals mirror the generic HMI CfgType enum.
 Append new values only.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NUMBER</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TEXT</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>BOOLEAN</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DURATION</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ TwinCAT binding name for Core TIME; TIME is a reserved keyword]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b — ONE value inside a parameter set, keyed by (Scope, WriteKey).

 This is the type that makes §3.8b's central prohibition structural. A byte
 image of a station's configuration - one aggregate memory-copied in and out -
 SHALL NOT be used, because it reinterprets retained bytes silently when a type
 changes, carries no per-value identity a file/database/MES can bind to, and
 cannot reject one bad value without rejecting all of them. A set built from
 these records has the opposite property on all three counts.

 Widths are not arbitrary: Scope is ST_ModuleStatus.Name, WriteKey is the
 §3.10.2 mutation identity, and ValueText is capped at the same 80 characters
 M_RegisterConfigWrite refuses to exceed for a text target - so a record can
 always carry any value the write path would have accepted.]]></Comment><BitSize>2720</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ owning module's canonical identity (= Status.Name)]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.10.2 mutation identity, scoped to that module]]></Comment><BitSize>1288</BitSize><BitOffs>648</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the capability revision the value was taken at]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1952</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1984</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ValueType</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigValueType</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2016</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ValueText</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ serialized exactly as a WRITE_CONFIG would carry it]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>2048</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigStore</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType>IQueryInterface</ExtendsType><Method><Name>M_Count</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ How many named sets this store holds, so a client can enumerate them.]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Delete</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Remove one named set. FALSE = no set of that name, or a save is open on it
 (a transaction is never pulled from under itself); nothing changed.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_InfoAt</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Header of the Index-th stored set, 1..M_Count, for a bounded listing.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_Kind</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Which medium is behind this store - published so an operator can see WHERE
 a saved set actually lives (§3.8b store table).]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigStore</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_ReadInfo</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Header of one stored set. FALSE = no set of that name (Info untouched).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ReadRecord</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One record of a stored set, addressed 1..Info.RecordCount. FALSE = absent
 set or out-of-range index (Record untouched).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SetName</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SaveAbort</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Discard an open save. Always safe to call, including when none is open.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_SaveBegin</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Open a save transaction for Info.SetName, overwriting any set of that name
 only when M_SaveCommit succeeds. FALSE = refused (no free slot, empty name,
 a save already open); nothing stored.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_SaveCommit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Close the save and make the set visible to a later read. FALSE = the set was
 not stored; the previous set of that name, if any, is left untouched.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_SaveRecord</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Append one record to the open save. FALSE = the set is full or no save is
