0184</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_CommandStyle</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.6.1 - how a published command is OPERATED, so a generic HMI can render
 it without knowing the module type (O1: no per-type HMI code).

 ONESHOT is the ordinary PLCopen command: press once, the module runs it to
 Done. HELD is a command that only acts while the operator keeps asking - a
 jog. The distinction is not cosmetic: a held action is re-asserted every scan
 and STOPS when the asking stops, including when it stops because the network
 stalled rather than because the operator let go (O10).]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>ONESHOT</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>HELD</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_CommandInfo</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.6.1 — one entry in a module's self-describing command catalog.
