 a value that must stay below another, a device that must be idle first. The
 base accepts; the framework still validates revision, type, range and domain
 and stores only after this returns TRUE. Two rules for an override: it shall
 have no side effects, because this runs on a candidate that may still be
 rejected; and it sees the RAW text, not a parsed value — 'abc' reaches it
 exactly as '7' does, so it must never assume the candidate is a number.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_TakeRestoreLoss</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b I_ConfigSource — hand the root this module's unreported restore loss,
