 client validates and writes back. Read live from the target every walk: a
 cached copy would let the manifest disagree with the machine.]]></Comment><ReturnType>STRING(255)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>2048</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Idx</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>pB</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BOOL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pI</Name><Type PointerTo="1">INT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pD</Name><Type PointerTo="1">DINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pU</Name><Type PointerTo="1">UDINT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pR</Name><Type PointerTo="1">REAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pL</Name><Type PointerTo="1">LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pT</Name><Type PointerTo="1">TIME</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pS</Name><Type PointerTo="1">STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyHeld</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1a I_ManualTarget - the held-command twin of M_ApplyManual. A type with
 no held commands inherits RequestHeldCommand's refusal, so an unsupported
 hold is a defined FALSE.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Enable</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ManualEnableStatus</Type><BitSize>664</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Cyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.1 — edge -> hooks -> dispatch -> map -> Execute-drop reset]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>commandStarted</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_CompositeModuleBase</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §2.2 / §8.2 — CM lifecycle + child registry + first-out rollup.
