 one module answers, and the first TRUE ends it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TextValue</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RootReady</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>iCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigSource</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_ReleaseCommand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §6.1/§8.3(b) — releasing a composite's command releases the whole subtree:
 a frozen chain leaves commands asserted at every tier it had reached, and any one
 of them left high blocks that module's next command edge. Recursive by
