 Execute in the step that issued it).]]></Comment><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyCapture</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8c - the capture walk is the write walk. Same order, same "first owner
 answers TRUE" rule, so a capture reaches exactly the module a write would.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Scope</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>WriteKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Revision</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RootReady</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>iCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigSource</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_TakeRestoreLoss</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — own loss first, then the children in registration order. One loss per
 call: the root drains until FALSE, so a subtree that lost several images
