Present</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>520</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>CarrierKind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_CarrierKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>544</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Result</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_PartResult</Type><BitSize>34944</BitSize><BitOffs>576</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Parents</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>4160</BitSize><BitOffs>35520</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_PartCarrier</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</ExtendsType><Method><Name>ReadContext</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ FALSE => caller faults with CARRIER_READ_FAILED (Core §3.16.2)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Ctx</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_PartContext</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>WriteResult</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ FALSE => caller faults with CARRIER_WRITE_FAILED; MUST precede EVENT_PART_PROCESSED]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Ctx</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_PartContext</Type><BitSize>39680</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigPersistence</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</ExtendsType><Method><Name>M_Cyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Drive the implementation; called every scan by the owning root. TRUE while a
 durability operation is still in progress, so the root can hold PersistPending
 exactly as long as the value really is not yet safe.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Failed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when the last completed operation did not make the data durable. Latched
 by the implementation until the next successful one: a failure that clears
 itself before anybody looks is not an answer to "is my configuration safe?".]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Request</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Ask for every write accepted so far to become durable. Returns FALSE if the
 request could not even be started, which is a failure the root publishes
 rather than a silent no-op. Safe to call while one is already in progress.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_EngineeringGate</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.5.1 — one ACTIVE commissioning/engineering gate in the station register.
 There is deliberately no `Active` member: a gate is a build constant (§7.5.1),
 so an inactive gate is not registered at all. A production station therefore
 publishes an EMPTY register, and the surfaces its gates control are invisible
 rather than merely disabled (§3.9).]]></Comment><BitSize>1936</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ stable gate identity, e.g. 'OUTPUT_FORCING']]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ localization key for the §7.5.2 annunciation]]></Comment><BitSize>1288</BitSize><BitOffs>648</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_EngineeringMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.5.1 — the station's commissioning/engineering gate register.

 A gate is any deliberate departure from the production configuration: a
 simulation driver in place of the real one, an unverified electrical mapping
 held off, untested logic fenced out — and the §10.5.1 output-force surface.
 Each is a BUILD constant (§7.5.1), so this register is written once at Setup
 and never changes at runtime: declaring a gate IS activating it, and an
 inactive gate is simply never declared. That is why ST_EngineeringGate has no
 `Active` member and why there is no cyclic call to forget (§1.1 O1) — a
 production image registers nothing and this whole surface is empty.

 One instance per station, in the composition root, injected into every root
 Unit with FB_UnitBase.SetEngineeringMode. Each Unit then raises the standing
 §7.5.2 annunciation for every registered gate: LOW, SYSTEM, AUTO_RESET,
 not shelvable, and closable only by a build without the gate.]]></Comment><BitSize>15616</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Gates</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_EngineeringGate</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>8</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>15488</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Count</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ 0 = a production image: nothing is gated, so nothing is annunciated and
 no gated surface is published. This is the value a released machine has.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>15552</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ForcingActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 rule 1 — the one gate the framework owns rather than the project.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>15568</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Truncated</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.5.1 bounded register: a station that declares more gates than the table
 holds would silently stop annunciating the rest, so say so instead (§5.6).]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>15576</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_forcingDeclared</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>15584</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>M_DeclareOutputForcing</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 rule 1 — register the framework's own force gate from the build
 constant. Called by FB_UnitBase.SetEngineeringMode, so a project that wires
 the register at all gets this gate declared without remembering a second call
 (§1.1 O1); a project that wires nothing simply cannot force (fail closed).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>slot</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_Declare</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.5.1 — register one ACTIVE gate; returns its slot (0 = not registered).
 `Active` is the caller's BUILD CONSTANT, taken as an input so a composition
 root reads as one line per gate with no IF around it:
     Engineering.M_Declare(Name := 'USE_SIMULATION',
         DescriptionKey := 'std.engineering.simulation', Active := USE_SIMULATION);
 Passing a runtime variable here defeats §7.5.1 and is a conformance defect,
 not a shortcut: a gate the machine can switch on is not auditable.]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Active</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_RunStyle</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.4.2 — how a running mode advances. HOLD_TO_RUN over HMI is NON-SAFETY.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>CONTINUOUS</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SINGLE_STEP</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>HOLD_TO_RUN</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_HostEvent</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §11.6.2 — transport-neutral fixed host-event record. Optional strings are
 empty when not applicable; Sequence gives a north-bound adapter stable ordering.]]></Comment><BitSize>4064</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Sequence</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Kind</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_HostEventKind</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>StationPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PartUid</Name><Type>STRING(64)</Type><BitSize>520</BitSize><BitOffs>2112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Subject</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ tool/resource/material identifier]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>2632</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ new mode/model/tool/material value]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>3280</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Stamp</Name><Type>DATE_AND_TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>3936</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TimeSynchronized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>3968</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Verdict</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Verdict</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>4000</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ReasonCode</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>4032</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_HostEventSink</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</ExtendsType><Method><Name>OnHostEvent</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Ev</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_HostEvent</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_PersistResult</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b - the outcome of one I_PersistMedium request.]]></Comment><BitSize>96</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ write: durable. read: the medium answered (Found or not)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Found</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ read: a valid, non-empty document was returned]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Lost</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ read: a document this medium confirmed writing is missing,]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Length</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ read: bytes returned]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ErrorId</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ last medium error (0 = none)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_PersistMedium</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</ExtendsType><Method><Name>M_Confidential</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when a document written here cannot be read back through the
 controller's symbol interfaces (ADS symbols, OPC UA). Only such a medium may
 hold credentials, even salted hashes (§14).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Kind</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The §3.8b medium class, published by a store built on this medium.]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigStore</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Poll</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Advance the medium and report on one ticket. TRUE = that request is finished
 and Result holds its outcome; the ticket is then released. An unknown ticket
 finishes at once with Ok = FALSE, so a caller can never wait forever.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Ticket</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Result</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_PersistResult</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_StartRead</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Queue a read of the newest valid document under Key into at most Size bytes
 at pData. 0 = refused, as for M_StartWrite.]]></Comment><ReturnType>UDINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pData</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Size</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_StartWrite</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Queue a write of Size bytes at pData under Key (letters, digits, '_', '.',
 '-'; at most 80). 0 = refused: an invalid key or size, or a full queue - ask
 again next scan. The bytes are taken when the write starts, not now.]]></Comment><ReturnType>UDINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Key</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pData</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Size</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_SignalTowerParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §8.13 — the site convention changes configuration, not mapping code.]]></Comment><BitSize>96</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LampTestDuration</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#3S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OperatorUsesWhite</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HornOnHigh</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_RecipeStore</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</ExtendsType><Method><Name>Save</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Replace the record of exactly (ModelCode, RecipeKey) with Size bytes at pData.
 FALSE when that record does not exist or its size or SchemaVersion differs:
 a fallback record is never edited in a specific model's name.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ModelCode</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RecipeKey</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>pData</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Size</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_HmiRequestKind</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.10/§14 — generic OPC UA request mailbox operation.
 Append-only: ordinal values are a transport contract with every HMI adapter.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LOGIN</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LOGOUT</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_MODE</Text><Enum>3</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_MODEL</Text><Enum>4</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>START</Text><Enum>5</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>STOP</Text><Enum>6</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONTROL_ON</Text><Enum>7</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CONTROL_OFF</Text><Enum>8</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>OPERATOR_RESET</Text><Enum>9</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DECISION_ANSWER</Text><Enum>10</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MANUAL_COMMAND</Text><Enum>11</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_RUN_STYLE</Text><Enum>12</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>STEP_REQUEST</Text><Enum>13</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_HOLD_RUN</Text><Enum>14</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RELEASE_START</Text><Enum>15</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RELEASE_MANUAL</Text><Enum>16</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RELEASE_ACTION</Text><Enum>17</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RESET_OEE</Text><Enum>18</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>WRITE_CONFIG</Text><Enum>19</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SHELVE_ALARM</Text><Enum>20</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>UNSHELVE_ALARM</Text><Enum>21</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FORCE_CHANNEL</Text><Enum>22</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>QUERY_CONFIG</Text><Enum>23</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.10.2 config-manifest page request (IntValue = page)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_ACCESS_LEVEL</Text><Enum>24</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.7 policy: IntValue=gate, TextValue=level ordinal]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_SESSION_TIMEOUT</Text><Enum>25</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.7 policy: DurationMs, 0 = never]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LAMP_TEST</Text><Enum>26</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.13 bounded signal-tower test]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CAPTURE_CONFIG</Text><Enum>27</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8c — a capture is a write whose value comes from the machine. The root
 already owned CaptureConfig; without a request kind no client could reach
 it, and §3.8c(a) requires a capture to be routed through this same
 acknowledged mailbox. TargetPath=Scope, NameValue=WriteKey, IntValue=rev.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SAVE_CONFIG_SET</Text><Enum>28</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b parameter sets. TextValue = set name; IntValue = E_ConfigKind for a
 save (which class of records the set carries). All three are CONFIG_SET,
 separately from the DATA_WRITE that edits one value.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LOAD_CONFIG_SET</Text><Enum>29</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>LIST_CONFIG_SETS</Text><Enum>30</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ACK_CONFIG_RESTORE</Text><Enum>31</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — an ENGINEER-level operator accepts a restore loss. Under
 BLOCK_UNTIL_ACKNOWLEDGED this is what releases START_STOP again.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EXPORT_CONFIG_SET</Text><Enum>32</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — move a set as TEXT. Export serves one JSON line per request
 (IntValue = line; 0 = header), import takes one back (TextValue = the line,
 BoolValue = this is the last one). Paged for the same reason QUERY_CONFIG
 is: no full set document ever has to exist in PLC memory. A line longer
 than TextValue travels in pieces: IntValue = 1 holds a piece, the next
 request without it completes the line (additive; an older root refuses a
 piece as an unreadable line, so it fails closed).]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>IMPORT_CONFIG_SET</Text><Enum>33</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>MANUAL_HELD</Text><Enum>34</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §7.6.1a hold-to-run. TargetPath = module, IntValue = command value,
 BoolValue = TRUE while the operator holds it. The client REFRESHES this
 while held; the root drops the hold on its own if refreshes stop, so a
 closed HMI or a dead link stops the motion rather than latching it.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DELETE_CONFIG_SET</Text><Enum>35</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b - remove one named set (TextValue = set name). CONFIG_SET, like the
 other set operations. Without it a store that has held MAX_CONFIG_SETS
 names could only ever overwrite one of them again.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SET_CLASS_LEVEL</Text><Enum>36</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8d - edit a data class's level. NameValue = ClassId, IntValue =
 E_AccessLevel ordinal, BoolValue = TRUE for the write level. ACCESS_POLICY.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CREATE_MODEL</Text><Enum>37</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Optional bounded catalog: inactive clone; NameValue = new code,
 IntValue = source model (0 running), BoolValue = from saved Model set,
 TextValue = source set name. Only offered with positive ModelCapacity.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EXPORT_CURRENT_CONFIG</Text><Enum>38</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Read-only snapshot export, TextValue = export name, IntValue = CfgKind,
