><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>2720</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_InfoAt</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_Kind</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ConfigStore</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">E_PersistentMode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Write persistent data control modes ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>SPDM_2PASS</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SPDM_VAR_BOOST</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_System">ADSWRITE</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ ADS write command. ]]></Comment><BitSize>1344</BitSize><SubItem><Name>NETID</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Ams net id ]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PORT</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsPort</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Ads communication port ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>IDXGRP</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Index group ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>IDXOFFS</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Index offset ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>LEN</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max. number of data bytes to write (LEN <= max. size of source buffer) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SRCADDR</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pointer to source buffer ]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property><Property><Name>TcIgnorePersistent</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>WRITE</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge starts command execution ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>448</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TMOUT</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Maximum time allowed for the execution of this ADS command ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>480</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>5000</DateTime></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BUSY</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Busy flag ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>512</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ERR</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Error flag ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>520</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ERRID</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ADS error code ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>544</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>hide_all_locals</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">FB_WritePersistentData</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This function block initiatializes storage of the persistent data from the PLC program ]]></Comment><BitSize>1728</BitSize><SubItem><Name>NETID</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TwinCAT network address (ams net id) ]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PORT</Name><Type>UINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Contains the ADS port number of the PLC run-time system whose persistent data is to be stored (851, 852...)]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>START</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge on this input activates the fb execution ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>272</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TMOUT</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max fb execution time ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>5000</DateTime></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MODE</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">E_PersistentMode</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ =SPDM_2PASS: optimized boost; =SPDM_VAR_BOOST: boost per variable; ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>E_PersistentMode.SPDM_2PASS</EnumText></Default><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BUSY</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>336</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ERR</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>344</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ERRID</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbAdsWrite</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">ADSWRITE</Type><BitSize>1344</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Default><SubItem><Name>.IDXGRP</Name><Value>139460625</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>.IDXOFFS</Name><Value>0</Value></SubItem></Default><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>conditionalshow_all_locals</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_PersistentDataWriter</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b — the SHIPPED DEFAULT durability provider for E_ConfigStore
 .LOCAL_RETAIN: it makes the PLC's retentive image reach non-volatile storage
 on demand, so an accepted configuration write is DURABLE and not merely LIVE.

 Why this exists at all: on TwinCAT the persistent image is written by the
 runtime, normally at a controlled shutdown. Every configuration write since
 the last write is therefore lost to a power cut - the station silently
 reverts at its next restart, which is exactly the failure §3.8b replaces with
 a stated property. Requesting the write explicitly turns that hope into an
 operation with a latency, a completion and a failure mode the root publishes.

 The ADS port is read from the runtime's own _AppInfo rather than hard-coded:
 a station on port 852 must not silently persist port 851's image.]]></Comment><BitSize>1920</BitSize><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ConfigPersistence</Implements><SubItem><Name>_writer</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">FB_WritePersistentData</Type><BitSize>1728</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_busy</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a write is in flight]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1856</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_queued</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a request arrived while one was in flight]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1864</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_failed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ latched until the next SUCCESSFUL write]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>1872</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>M_Request</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ A write already in flight cannot be told about a value accepted after it
 started, so a request arriving now is QUEUED rather than merged: the value
 gets its own write and PersistPending stays TRUE until that one finishes.
 Merging them is the bug that reports a value durable which was never written.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Failed</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>M_Cyclic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Drive the ADS write. Returns TRUE while data is still not durable, which is
 what the root publishes as PersistPending.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ConfigSetJson</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8b — the TEXT projection of a parameter set: one JSON object per
 record, one per header. This is what makes a set MOVABLE - to a file, to a
 version-control system, to an asset manager, to another controller - which is
 the whole point of having named sets rather than just retentive memory.

 FORMAT DECISION (JSON, and per RECORD rather than per document):

   * JSON over XML because the consumers are a Flutter HMI, a Dart gateway and
     ordinary MES tooling, all of which parse it natively; nothing in the set
     needs attributes, namespaces or mixed content.

   * Per RECORD, because §3.8b's central prohibition is the byte image, and
     the stated reasons are that it carries no per-value identity to bind to
     and cannot reject one bad value without rejecting all of them. A
     line-per-record document keeps both properties in the serialization
     itself: every line is independently identified by (scope, key) and
     independently rejectable. A single monolithic JSON document would parse
     back to the same records, but a PLC-side parser for one would need an
     unbounded buffer and would fail the whole file on one bad character -
     which is the byte image again, in a friendlier syntax.

   * A line is emitted or refused, NEVER truncated. A line may be 480
     characters wide, but the standard string functions (CONCAT, LEN, FIND,
     MID) are specified to 255 and silently cut there, even into a wider
     target - measured on the runtime, where a 330-character record rendered
     as 255 bytes. So nothing here uses them on a line: _M_Put appends byte by
     byte and REFUSES at the width, _M_Length and _M_Find scan to the
     terminator, and an over-long line produces an empty string the caller
     must handle, not a silently shortened value (§5.6).

 The projection is pure: no state, no I/O, no allocation. Writing the lines to
 a file, an ADS client or an MES connector is a deployment adapter's job
 (§3.15), not the framework's.]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><SubItem><Name>LINE_MAX</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ A record line holds a STRING(80) scope, a STRING(160) key, a STRING(80)
 value with every character escaped, and ~70 characters of fixed syntax.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><Value>480</Value></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>_M_Length</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The length of a zero-terminated line, by scanning - LEN stops seeing a
 string at 255. Bounded by LINE_MAX, so a missing terminator cannot run away.]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pText</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Put</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Append the zero-terminated text at pText to Line (Used bytes long). FALSE -
 and Line exactly as it was - when the result would exceed LINE_MAX: the
 append is measured first, so it is whole or not at all.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pText</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Line</Name><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Used</Name><Type ReferenceTo="true">INT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>pOut</Name><Type PointerTo="1">BYTE</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_PutText</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ _M_Put for a short literal or number (at most 255 characters).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Line</Name><Type ReferenceTo="true">STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Used</Name><Type ReferenceTo="true">INT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_Header</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Render the set header as a JSON object. The timestamp is emitted as the
 §2.7 clock's seconds value rather than a formatted date: a set document is
 machine input, and a numeric instant cannot be misread by a reader in another
 locale. TimeSynchronized travels with it, so a consumer can tell a trustworthy
 instant from one stamped while the clock had lost its source.]]></Comment><ReturnType>STRING(480)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>3848</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Info</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ConfigSetInfo</Type><BitSize>2016</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>nameText</Name><Type>STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>3848</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rootText</Name><Type>STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>3848</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>modelText</Name><Type>STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>3848</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>line</Name><Type>STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>3848</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>used</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_ParseRecord</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Parse one record line back into a record. FALSE = the line is not a record
 line this build understands, and NOTHING in Record has been changed.

 This is untrusted input in the fullest sense - it may have been edited by
 hand, produced by another vendor's tool, or moved between machines - so it is
 parsed into a record and then still validated by the owning module's typed
 handler before any value changes (§5.6, §14). Getting a well-formed record
 out of here proves the SYNTAX, never the value.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Line</Name><Type>STRING(480)</Type><BitSize>3848</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Record</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ConfigRecord</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>scopeText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>keyText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>valueText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>revText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>kindText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>typeText</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>revValue</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>kindValue</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>typeValue</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_ParseHeader</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §3.8b — parse a set HEADER line. FALSE = not a header (no "set" member), or
 one this build cannot make sense of; Info is untouched either way.

 A header and a record are unambiguous by shape - a header carries "set" and a
 record carries "key", and neither carries the other - so a caller can offer a
