 project hardware driver with its owning Unit's FB_UnitBase.M_ForcePermitted().

 The falling edge is what makes the rule real: leaving MANUAL, starting a mode,
 or a build without the §7.5 gate WITHDRAWS every force rather than leaving a
 set-point contending with live application logic. Deriving the edge from the
 published flag itself (not from instance state) keeps every publisher attached
 to this table in agreement about whether a force is live.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Enabled</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_DefineAnalogChannel</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.5.1 — declare a non-boolean channel: an analog input, or the process-image
 bytes of a communication terminal (an EL6001 status/data byte is a channel of
 the bus like any other, and an operator diagnosing a dead link needs to see it).
 Identical validation to M_DefineDigitalChannel; only Kind and the unit differ.
 The unit has ONE source per channel: a UnitCode (the published Unit text is then
 derived from it), or - only for a unit E_EngUnit lacks - EngUnit text. A channel
 given both is a mapping defect and is refused, never silently resolved.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Tag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Address</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Path</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModulePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ChannelDir</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>EngUnit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ '' with a UnitCode, or when the raw count has no unit]]></Comment><Type>STRING(16)</Type><BitSize>136</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>UnitCode</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ E_EngUnit.NONE when the unit is given as EngUnit text]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_EngUnit</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_EffectiveBool</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 — the value the hardware driver should actually write to this
 digital output: the held force set-point while forcing is permitted, otherwise
 the application's own value. It RETURNS the value, so a driver line still reads
 as a plain assignment (the same shape as _M_State on a module):

     GVL_PressIO._101K301A := _publisher.M_EffectiveBool(
         NodeIndex := 4, ChannelIndex := 1, Value := SlideHal.ExtendOut);

 An out-of-range or unforced channel returns Value unchanged, so a mapping
 mistake degrades to ordinary control rather than to a stuck output (§5.6).]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_EffectiveAnalog</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 — the analog twin of M_EffectiveBool, same contract.]]></Comment><ReturnType>REAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Value</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyDiagnostic</Name><Parameter><Name>Diagnostic</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_DefineNode</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>TypeId</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Address</Name><Type>STRING(40)</Type><BitSize>328</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ParentIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_Reject</Name><Parameter><Name>Text</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_ApplyDiagnosticToTag</Name><Parameter><Name>Diagnostic</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Tag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_DefineDigitalChannel</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Tag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Address</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Path</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModulePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ChannelDir</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_BeginDiagnosticRefresh</Name><Local><Name>n</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_PressIoCatalog</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Owner-local I/O engineering-data adapter. This is the ONE source for the approved
