 up on it), appended to the owning root's manifest. The Unit reaches the
 topology through the catalog it was given, never through the global itself.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Pager</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">FB_ConfigPager</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_DefineCylinder</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ModulePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendedSensorTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendedSensorDescription</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendedSensorAddress</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendedSensorIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractedSensorTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractedSensorDescription</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractedSensorAddress</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractedSensorIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendOutputTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendOutputDescription</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendOutputAddress</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendOutputIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractOutputTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractOutputDescription</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractOutputAddress</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractOutputIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ExtendedTimeoutKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>RetractedTimeoutKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>BothSensorsKey</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_CylinderIoIdentity</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>M_RouteForce</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 — apply one accepted force request to the approved channel join
 this catalog owns (§10.2.1). Every authority check upstream of the physical
 contract has already happened in FB_UnitBase.ForceChannel; the publisher
 rechecks root ownership, OUTPUT direction and the Forceable capability, and
 refuses anything else. This writes only the held set-point: the hardware
 driver decides each scan whether set-points are applied at all.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ChannelPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>OwnerRootPath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Force</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>BoolValue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>AnalogValue</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_DefineIdentity</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Identity</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IoPointIdentity</Type><BitSize>6680</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ChannelDir</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_M_DefinePoint</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>NodeIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ChannelIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Tag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>DescriptionKey</Name><Type>STRING(160)</Type><BitSize>1288</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Address</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ModulePath</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Dir</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ChannelDir</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>Path</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_DeclareForceable</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §10.5.1 rule 1 — mark the outputs this station allows to be forced from
 the HMI, and ONLY while the §7.5 OUTPUT_FORCING build gate is active.

 Two channels of the EL2809 are deliberately excluded even in a commissioning
 image: =000+S-K010C1 Ch10/Ch11 (_000K951_A1 / _000K911_A1) drive the hardwired
 N54 D2 Control On relay chain. That chain is this machine's control-power
 authority, and §10.5.1 rule 4 keeps the standard-PLC force surface out of
 anything with that role. Forcing them would energize control power from a
 diagnostic screen, which is exactly the act this surface must never offer.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Engineering</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">FB_EngineeringMode</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>c</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>allow</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>Ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_PneumaticPressParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8 ParCfg (SchemaVersion first; adding a member = schema change).
 v2 adds the §8.11 performance references: per-model ideal cycle (OEE
 Performance denominator, §8.5.1) and the WORK-time degradation baseline
 (§8.11.4(d); 0 = watch off).

 v3 REMOVES RequireTwoHandStart. It was recipe data in name only - every one of
 the four catalog records set it TRUE - and §3.8a's test is whether the value
 changes with the model. It does not: it answers whether this CELL's risk
 assessment demands a two-hand start, which is deployment data and now lives in
 ST_PneumaticPressStationCfg. A recipe that could switch it off would let a
 changeover quietly remove a required operator protection.

 TransferSettleTime deliberately STAYED. Its catalog values genuinely differ per
 model (80/100/120/150 ms): a heavier steel blank settles on the slide more
 slowly than a plastic one, so it is a fact about the part, not the mechanism.]]></Comment><BitSize>160</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>3</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PressSettleTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#500MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TransferSettleTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#100MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>IdealCycleMs</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.5.1 — 0 = Performance not computed]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BaselineWorkMs</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ §8.11.4(d) — 0 = degradation watch off]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_PneumaticPressParCmd</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reserved</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ControlModule</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_Module</ExtendsType><Method><Name>AbortCommand</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>ExecuteCommand</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Command</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ value of the type's E_<Type>Command]]></Comment><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceId</Name><Value>2151</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §2.2 — leaf-tier semantic base. The shared PLCopen lifecycle lives in
 FB_ModuleBase; this type supplies only the Control Module tier identity.]]></Comment><BitSize>265472</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ModuleBase</ExtendsType><Implements Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_ControlModule</Implements><Method><Name>__getModuleType</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ModuleType</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>ModuleType</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_ModuleType</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_CylinderCommand</Name><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>NONE</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>EXTEND</Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>RETRACT</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderParCfg</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §3.8: SchemaVersion FIRST, initialized to the expected version. v2 appended
 the valve-timing members; every default reproduces v1. A zero time is "off" and
 never conflicts; a non-zero SettleTime or MinOutputTime must be shorter than
 MoveTimeout, and PulsingWidth shorter than PulsingPeriod (CYL_CFG_INVALID).]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><SubItem><Name>SchemaVersion</Name><Type>UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MoveTimeout</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#2S</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SettleTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ end sensor confirmed continuously before Done]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#0MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MinOutputTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a move is commanded at least this long before Done]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#0MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PulsingWidth</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ a move started from no end position pulses its coil...]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#0MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PulsingPeriod</Name><Type>TIME</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ ...for PulsingWidth of every PulsingPeriod, until the target makes]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#0MS</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ResetOnEndPos</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ withdraw the coil at Done (impulse/bistable valves); FALSE holds it]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ResetOnTimeout</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ withdraw the coil when the move times out]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderParCmd</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reserved</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderOutCmd</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Reached</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderOutImm</Name><BitSize>2608</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Extended</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Retracted</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ExtendedSensorTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RetractedSensorTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>664</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ExtendOutputTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>1312</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RetractOutputTag</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>1960</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IntlkCond</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.2 — per-condition record of FB_PermIntlk]]></Comment><BitSize>2144</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Defined</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Description</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ localization key]]></Comment><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2080</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Bypassable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2112</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_PermIntlk</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.2 — the standard permissive/interlock container: fixed container,
 author-chosen condition language (LD/ST/FBD drive Cond[i], TRUE = OK).
 First FALSE, non-bypassed, defined condition is the first-out reason (Core §6.9).]]></Comment><BitSize>40320</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Cond</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>16</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ author drives these (TRUE = OK)]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AllOk</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ every defined, non-bypassed condition is TRUE]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AnyBypassed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ at least one defined condition is bypassed]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>FirstFailed</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ lowest index of a FALSE, non-bypassed condition; 0 = none]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_conds</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_IntlkCond</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>16</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>34304</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_bypass</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>16</Elements></ArrayInfo><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>34528</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_diag</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize><BitOffs>34656</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_lastFf</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>40224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>40240</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ok</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>40256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>byp</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>40264</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ff</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>40272</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Define</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.2 — declare one condition record (typically once, in the owner's Setup/init).
 Bounds-checked per Core §5.6: an out-of-range index is rejected, never written.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Description</Name><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Reason</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">E_Reason</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Bypassable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ClearBypass</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.2 — clears all bypasses]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>__getDiagnostic</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.2 — first-out: Reason + Description of FirstFailed (ReasonCode = NONE when AllOk)]]></Comment><ReturnType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>5568</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>Diagnostic</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_Diagnostic</Type><BitSize>5568</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>SetBypass</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.2/§7.3 — succeeds only for a defined, explicitly-bypassable condition]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Index</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>On</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>AppendFailed</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Core §7.8 — append EVERY currently-failed (defined, non-bypassed, FALSE) condition
 to a release report as INTERLOCK reasons. Returns the new count. Complete list,
 not just first-out. Pure query: never commands, never mutates conditions.]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>SourcePath</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ owner supplied explicitly; the container is reusable]]></Comment><Type>STRING(255)</Type><BitSize>2048</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_ValveDrive</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The coil level of ONE commanded valve move, written once so every cylinder type
 drives its coils the same way. Owner-private: no module identity, no published
 state, no I/O - the owner writes the level it returns, and keeps every decision
 that is not timing (which coil, interlocks, HELD, abort, end-of-move reset).

 A move that pulses switches its coil on for PulsingWidth at the start of every
 PulsingPeriod until the owner reports its target confirmed; any other move holds
 the coil on. MinTimeElapsed reports that the move has been commanded for at
 least MinOutputTime, for valves that cannot switch faster than that.]]></Comment><BitSize>640</BitSize><SubItem><Name>MinTimeElapsed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_pulsing</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ this move pulses until its target is confirmed]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tMin</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ since the move began]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tPeriod</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the running pulse period]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>M_Begin</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Start a move: the scan the owner first energizes the coil.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Pulsing</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>MinOutputTime</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>__getPulsing</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Whether this move was begun as a pulsing move.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>Pulsing</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>M_Coil</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The coil level for this scan of the move begun by M_Begin. Steady holds the coil
 on (the target is confirmed); when pulsing resumes, it starts with a full pulse.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>Steady</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>PulsingWidth</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>PulsingPeriod</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>M_Reset</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Drops pulsing, timers and minimum time elapsed.]]></Comment></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderCM</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Annex A/B pattern on the base class: the type is ONLY its device logic.
 Valve timing (ParCfg v2) is configuration, never a weaker stop: OnAbort always
 de-energizes, a lost interlock always HOLDS with both coils off, and a coil the
 owner withdrew stays off until RestoreOutputs or the next move - whatever the
 pulsing, minimum-output or end-of-move settings say.]]></Comment><BitSize>327744</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_ControlModuleBase</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>Command</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">E_CylinderCommand</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>265472</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCfg</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderParCfg</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>265504</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ParCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderParCmd</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>265728</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutCmd</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderOutCmd</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>265736</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OutImm</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderOutImm</Type><BitSize>2608</BitSize><BitOffs>265744</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Intlk</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_PermIntlk</Type><BitSize>40320</BitSize><BitOffs>268352</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_hal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules" ReferenceTo="true">ST_CylinderHal</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>308672</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_recipe</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">I_RecipeProvider</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>308736</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>OPC.UA.DA</Name><Value>0</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tMove</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>308800</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_tSettle</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>309056</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_drive</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_ValveDrive</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ the commanded coil's level for this move]]></Comment><BitSize>640</BitSize><BitOffs>309312</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_withdrawn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ WithdrawOutputs is the owner's functional stop. A pulsed move writes its coil
 every scan, so the stop is latched here until RestoreOutputs or a new move.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>309952</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_holdCoil</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The level the commanded coil keeps outside a move: FALSE only after a Done
