 same report the HMI displays, so this condition cannot become explanation-only.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Report</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" ReferenceTo="true">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>ConfigurePartFeedAxis</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Bind the NC axis for the part-feed servo and arm the module.

 Called from OnCyclic until it succeeds, so the axis arms itself the moment an
 NC axis is linked and stays dormant forever on a bench without one. It is
 idempotent and fails closed on both an invalid reference and an unlinked one
 (AxisId 0), which is what makes calling it every scan safe.

 The drive is a Jenny Science XENAX Xvi over EtherCAT/CiA402 on the DEV PC's
 own bus - a stand-in for a feed axis, not press cabinet hardware. See the
 note on PartFeedAxis.

 The conditions are declared HERE rather than in FB_PressDemoRelease only
 because the axis is not yet in the AUTO chain. When it joins the chain they
 belong beside the other project permits in the Release object, which S7.2.1
 prefers as a single visible component, and this method should shrink to
 binding the reference.

 ParCfg limits are deliberately NOT set here. Soft limits, velocity and
 acceleration come from the axis configuration and the recipe (S10.3); a Unit
 that hard-codes a stroke is wrong the first time the mechanics change.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>AxisRef</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_MC2" ReferenceTo="true">AXIS_REF</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnInit</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ First operational scan: initialize application-owned mode-chain state.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>_M_WithdrawSequenceOutputs</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One safe-stop wiring point shared by normal and error-state abort transitions.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>SetIoCatalog</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §10.2.1 — inject this station's I/O catalog so §10.5.1 force requests can be
 resolved against the approved engineering-data join instead of against a
 second copy of the channel map. Wired once by the composition root.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>Catalog</Name><Type ReferenceTo="true">FB_PressIoCatalog</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>OnOperatorReset</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ An operator reset is recovering this Unit: put the application back to the same
 safe wiring an error-state abort establishes, so the reset the operator presses at
 the panel needs no separate Stop/Abort first. The base then releases the run
 command and the children's commands, so the next HOME gets a genuine command edge.
 Unlike the abort paths this does NOT touch control power in either direction: it
 never requests Control On (§9.8 forbids self-resume), and it must not request
 Control Off either — powering down a healthy control circuit would make the
 operator re-enable it before HOME could run, i.e. reintroduce the multi-action
 recovery this reset exists to remove. Power stays where the operator put it.]]></Comment><ReturnType>DINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderSim</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ §5.7 per-type sim plant model: drives the HAL feedback with a travel time —
