Hal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019520</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DoorHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019552</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SlideHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019584</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TwoHandHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_TwoHandHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019616</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PowerHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_PowerGroupHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019648</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PartPresentHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputHal</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>39019680</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AirPressureHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureHal</Type><BitSize>24</BitSize><BitOffs>39019696</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PressSim</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderSim</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>39019776</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DoorSim</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderSim</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>39020480</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SlideSim</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderSim</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>39021184</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Recipe</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalRecipeProvider</Type><BitSize>173184</BitSize><BitOffs>39021888</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Fast</Name><Type>ST_PneumaticPressParCfg</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize><BitOffs>39195072</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Slow</Name><Type>ST_PneumaticPressParCfg</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize><BitOffs>39195232</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SlowModel</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ModelId</Type><BitSize>7856</BitSize><BitOffs>39195392</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Domain</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ControlDomainStatus</Type><BitSize>137376</BitSize><BitOffs>39203264</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Release</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>100640</BitSize><BitOffs>39340640</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Wired</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>39441280</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>39441296</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Model_changeover_is_transactional</Name></Method><Method><Name>Start_release_enforces_operating_air</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Press example of Core T10: an immediate mode-entry permissive is both
 explainable and enforced. Part/two-hand remain future AUTO step conditions.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>Auto_cycle_returns_to_load_position</Name><Local><Name>beforeRam</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>beforeDoor</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>beforeSlide</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>firstGood</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_CommandCount</Name><ReturnType>UDINT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>pTiming</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core" PointerTo="1">ST_ModuleTiming</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>CommandId</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>rowIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Home_and_changeover_sequences_are_explicit</Name></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_FaultRecovery_Tests</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Regression suite for the press hard-lock: an AUTO cycle reached N200 (ram down),
 the operator released the two-hand button mid-stroke — the designed way to stop a
 stroke — and NO panel action could recover the machine.

 Measured on the live PLC, the lock was two latches deep:
   1. the lost permissive was classified as a FAULT, so the only exit was
      Reset -> IDLE, and the fault's own condition ("two-hand held during a
      stroke") could only be re-established by starting;
   2. OperatorReset skipped an ACTIVE event and left both Execute inputs asserted,
      and §6.1's Execute-drop reset — the sole exit from a latched terminal state —
      needs them low. A Unit that is not BUSY never calls _M_Dispatch again, so the
      frozen step holding `PressRam.Execute := TRUE` could never clear it, and the
      next HOME re-issued an already-TRUE input: no rising edge, ram stuck in its
      latched state, Unit re-adopting the fault through the §8.2 rollup.

 The ram is held mid-stroke deterministically by NOT calling its sim plant, so its
 position feedback never arrives (MoveTimeout is T#2S and a TON cannot advance
 inside one PLC scan, so it cannot expire here and turn the wait into a timeout).]]></Comment><BitSize>39433280</BitSize><ExtendsType Namespace="TcUnit">FB_TestSuite</ExtendsType><SubItem><Name>Press</Name><Type>FB_PressDemoUnit</Type><BitSize>5444608</BitSize><BitOffs>33574912</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PressHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019520</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DoorHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019552</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SlideHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_CylinderHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019584</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TwoHandHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_TwoHandHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019616</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PowerHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_PowerGroupHal</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>39019648</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PartPresentHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_DigitalInputHal</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>39019680</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AirPressureHal</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">ST_AirPressureHal</Type><BitSize>24</BitSize><BitOffs>39019696</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PressSim</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderSim</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>39019776</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DoorSim</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderSim</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>39020480</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SlideSim</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Modules">FB_CylinderSim</Type><BitSize>704</BitSize><BitOffs>39021184</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Recipe</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">FB_LocalRecipeProvider</Type><BitSize>173184</BitSize><BitOffs>39021888</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Cfg</Name><Type>ST_PneumaticPressParCfg</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize><BitOffs>39195072</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Domain</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ControlDomainStatus</Type><BitSize>137376</BitSize><BitOffs>39195232</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Release</Name><Type Namespace="Fraktal_Core">ST_ReleaseReport</Type><BitSize>100640</BitSize><BitOffs>39332608</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Wired</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>39433248</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>39433264</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>Latched_fault_recovers_with_one_operator_reset</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Defect A + C, the actual hard-lock: a genuine fault while the ram is travelling
 left a state the press could not get out of. ONE reset has to make HOME runnable
 again. The fault is a contradictory door position (both end sensors) while the
 door closes - a defect, unlike air loss, which the process restores and which
 therefore holds (Air_loss_mid_stroke_holds_and_resumes).]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>Two_hand_release_mid_stroke_holds_the_ram</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Defect B: releasing the button mid-stroke is expected operator behaviour, so it
 belongs in HELD (suspend, resume when restored), not in a fault whose only exit is
 Reset -> IDLE. Nothing is relaxed: the output is still withheld by the same permit.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_AtStep</Name><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>StepNo</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>branchIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rowIndex</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_RunToRamDown</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Drive the fixture from the load-safe position to N200 with the ram commanded
 EXTEND and still travelling. The ram's plant model is deliberately NOT ticked, so
 its extended feedback never arrives and the stroke stays in progress.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>scan</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>_M_ReturnToIdle</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Leave the fixture where every test in this suite expects to find it: AUTO, stopped,
 no blocking event, ram/door/slide back at the load-safe position, two-hand released.]]></Comment><Local><Name>scan</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Two_hand_release_in_the_dwell_holds_and_restores</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ N220 holds the press force through the dwell. The force is the valve latched by the
 EXTEND that N200 already completed, so a withdraw needs an explicit restore — the
 case a hold at the CM alone does not cover.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>_M_RunToDoorClosing</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Drive the fixture to N180 with the door commanded EXTEND and still travelling.
 N180 AWAITS the door, so a door fault there is adopted by the Unit through the
 rollup (§8.2) - unlike N200, which owns the ram's failure itself. The door's
 plant model is deliberately NOT ticked, so its closed feedback never arrives.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>scan</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>Reset_never_bypasses_a_live_condition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The reset closes a latched event even while a start condition is unsatisfied, which
 is only safe because it clears the LATCH and never the condition. Proof: fault the
 Unit, take the air away, reset, then watch the release report keep Start shut on
 that live condition.]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>Air_loss_mid_stroke_holds_and_resumes</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Air is restored by the process, not repaired, so losing it mid-stroke is HELD
 (§6.1): the ram's own process condition withdraws its valve, the Unit reports the
 hold by name, nothing is latched, and the stroke resumes when pressure returns.]]></Comment></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name GUID="{302277DD-5AD1-433D-B776-5031AECC2BB4}" TcBaseType="true">EPlcPersistentStatus</Name><BitSize>8</BitSize><BaseType GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000002}">USINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text><![CDATA[PS_None]]></Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text><![CDATA[PS_All]]></Text><Enum>1</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text><![CDATA[PS_Partial]]></Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><Hides><Hide GUID="{4591E628-DBCE-4E33-AE0B-7EB853AA256E}" /></Hides></DataType><DataType><Name GUID="{D8713831-B59F-4201-84CC-04357A7EE4B7}" TcBaseType="true">PlcAppSystemInfo</Name><BitSize>2048</BitSize><SubItem><Name>ObjId</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-00000000000F}">OTCID</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>TaskCnt</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000008}">UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OnlineChangeCnt</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000008}">UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Flags</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000007}">DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AdsPort</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000005}">UINT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BootDataLoaded</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000030}">BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>144</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>OldBootData</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000030}">BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>152</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AppTimestamp</Name><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-00000000004C}">DT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><