 real memory cost per chain, not a loop limit (§1.1 O10: statically sized,
 no run-time allocation). Legs are numbered 1..n; 0 is the main line and is
 always available on top of these.]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>9</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641628416</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_Fraktal.WINDOWS_CLOCK_SAMPLE_FILE</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TC3 Windows observer default, also emitted into the observer package.]]></Comment><BitSize>2048</BitSize><BaseType>STRING(255)</BaseType><Default><String>C:\ProgramData\Fraktal\Clock\quality.bin</String></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641628432</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>PL_ReasonCatalog.COUNT</Name><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><Default><Value>97</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>TcVarGlobal</Name></Property></Properties><BitOffs>641630480</BitOffs></Symbol><Symbol><Name>GVL_FraktalTime.Current</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ One PLC-wide clock-quality authority. Hidden here; each root republishes
